<title>CHINA: Bank loans for projects in China's Shenzhen.</title>
<headline>Bank loans for projects in China's Shenzhen.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eleven Chinese banks have pledged to extend 1.54 billion yuan ($185.5 million) in loans to 19 key construction projects in China's southern boomtown of Shenzhen, the Xinhua news agency said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Shenzhen envisages a total of 44 key projects estimated to cost 12.95 billion yuan this year, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>The projects include the West Power Plant, the second phase of Yantian port, a telecommunications hub and an optical fibre programme, it said, without giving further details.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
